              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 2s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Before the new one: say the Marathi for to present, then the Marathi for to host a programme."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: कार्य",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "कार्य — kārya — \"a task; a function\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "हे कार्य आज संध्याकाळपर्यंत पूर्ण झालं. he kārya āj sandhyākāḷparyant pūrṇa jhālaṁ. This task was finished by this evening."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Neuter."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "कार्य (kārya) is a tatsama, taken from Sanskrit kārya, \"what is to be done, work\" (Monier-Williams)."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for describing what you lived and felt."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
